    {
      "id": "kpk1-l18-b2-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l18-b2-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Miasto, w mieście"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Before the *-e* of the locative, some sounds change: *t* becomes *ci*, *d* becomes *dzi*, *s* becomes *si*, *ł* becomes *l*, and often *a* becomes *e* and *ó* becomes *o* as well. So *miasto* is *w mieście*, *las* is *w lesie*, *świat* is *na świecie*, *kościół* is *w kościele*, and *obiad* is *po obiedzie*. The locative also follows *o* (about) and *po* (after). Learn three apart: *dom*, *w domu*; *pan*, *o panu*; *syn*, *o synu*."
      },
      "table": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Uwaga!"
        },
